            <ArticleTitle>A general approach for nanoparticle composite transport materials toward efficient perovskite solar cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11028-11031</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05934e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The design of electron transport layers (ETLs) is crucial to the performance of optoelectronic devices. A composite ETL was constructed to overcome the poor carrier extraction issue in perovskite solar cells, resulting in a maximum PCE of 19.14% with reduced hysteresis. A similar enhancement phenomenon was observed in both devices based on TiO2 and SnO2 ETLs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
